{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Find the current official Prodigi Print API v4 documentation for: creating an order, sandbox/test mode behavior, product SKU/catalog for a standard black t-shirt with sizes S/M/L/XL, artwork URL requirements, and authentication. Return exact endpoint paths, request field names, and any important restrictions. Prefer official prodigi.com developer docs."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Find the current official Prodigi Print API v4 documentation for: creating an order, sandbox/test mode behavior, product SKU/catalog for a standard black t-shirt with sizes S/M/L/XL, artwork URL requirements, and authentication. Return exact endpoint paths, request field names, and any important restrictions. Prefer official prodigi.com developer docs."},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research Report: Prodigi Print API v4 Documentation\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThe Prodigi Print API v4 provides a comprehensive set of endpoints for creating and managing print orders, operating in both sandbox and live environments. Key functionalities include order creation, authentication via API keys, and detailed product specifications, such as SKUs for standard black t-shirts in sizes S, M, L, and XL. The API also outlines requirements for artwork URLs and supports multiple image formats.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **Finding 1:** The API supports both sandbox and live environments, allowing developers to test orders without charges in the sandbox environment before moving to live production. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 2:** Authentication is managed through an `X-API-Key` header, with separate keys required for sandbox and live environments. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 3:** The API accepts artwork in JPG, PNG, or PDF formats, requiring a full URL path to the image asset, which can be public or a private signed URL. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/blog/your-first-print-api-order/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 4:** For standard black t-shirts available in sizes S, M, L, and XL, the API provides specific SKUs and attributes, including available print areas and color options. ([dashboard.dev.kitely.prodigi.tech](https://dashboard.dev.kitely.prodigi.tech/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Source Analysis\n\n### Source 1: Prodigi API Documentation\n\n- **URL:** [https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/)\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Official Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official API documentation from Prodigi)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Prodigi API Documentation provides a comprehensive reference for version 4 of their print API. It details the RESTful API structure, including standard HTTP response codes, authentication methods, and supported HTTP verbs. The documentation outlines the two available environments: Sandbox for testing without charges and Live for actual order fulfillment. Authentication is managed via an `X-API-Key` header, with separate keys for each environment. The order creation process is described, including the structure of the Order object, which encompasses recipient details, items, and assets. The API accepts artwork in JPG, PNG, or PDF formats, requiring a full URL path to the image asset. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/?utm_source=openai))\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Sandbox API URL: `api.sandbox.prodigi.com`\n\n- Live API URL: `api.prodigi.com`\n\n- Authentication header: `X-API-Key`\n\n- Supported image formats: JPG, PNG, PDF\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Each request to our API requires the use of an authentication header: `X-API-Key`.\"\n\n> \"We have two environments: Sandbox and Live.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 2: How to Place your First Order with the Prodigi Print API\n\n- **URL:** [https://www.prodigi.com/blog/your-first-print-api-order/](https://www.prodigi.com/blog/your-first-print-api-order/)\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** March 18, 2021\n\n- **Source Type:** Blog Post\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official blog post from Prodigi)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThis blog post guides users through placing their first order using the Prodigi Print API v4. It emphasizes the importance of acquiring an API key, selecting a product, sourcing an image, and submitting an order. The post provides a sample order creation request, highlighting the necessity of including a full URL path to the image asset, which can be public or a private signed URL. It also notes that the API accepts artwork in JPG, PNG, or PDF formats. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/blog/your-first-print-api-order/?utm_source=openai))\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Sample SKU: `GLOBAL-FAP-16x24`\n\n- Sample image URL: `https://your-image-url/image.png`\n\n- Supported image formats: JPG, PNG, PDF\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"We require a full URL path to this image asset as part of creating the order, at either a public or a private signed URL.\"\n\n> \"We accept jpg and png format images. For some products we may recommend one format over the other.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 3: Print API Reference\n\n- **URL:** [https://dashboard.dev.kitely.prodigi.tech/docs/](https://dashboard.dev.kitely.prodigi.tech/docs/)\n\n- **Domain:** kitely.prodigi.tech\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Developer Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** Medium (Developer documentation from Prodigi)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThis documentation provides detailed information on product templates, including applicable positions, available colors, and sizes for various apparel items. For standard black t-shirts available in sizes S, M, L, and XL, it specifies the SKU as `aa_mens_tshirt` with print areas on the center chest and center back. The available colors include black, white, and heather grey. ([dashboard.dev.kitely.prodigi.tech](https://dashboard.dev.kitely.prodigi.tech/docs/?utm_source=openai))\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Product SKU: `aa_mens_tshirt`\n\n- Available sizes: S, M, L, XL\n\n- Available colors: black, white, heather grey\n\n- Print areas: center_chest, center_back\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"All apparel orders must be made with options and sizes that correspond to the product ordered as detailed in the below table.\"\n\n> \"Product Template: `aa_mens_tshirt` | Applicable Positions: center_chest, center_back | Available Colors: black, white, heather_grey | Available Sizes: s,m,l,xl\"\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Reference Analysis\n\n**Consensus Across Sources:**\n\n- � "}],"_meta":{"openai/widgetSessionId":"86cb596a-3949-4e43-ad0d-f7c2f73d5817"},"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
