class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"10.74\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\">\n663-                </span><span class=\"nl\">\"currency\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"GBP\"</span><span class=\"w\">\n664-            </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\">\n665-        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\">\n666-    </span><span class=\"p\">],</span><span class=\"w\">\n--\n737-<td>array of <a href=\"#order-object-shipment\" title=\"Order shipments\">Shipments</a></td>\n738-<td>n/a</td>\n739-<td>Courier and service shipment details per item, if available. Set by Prodigi.</td>\n740-</tr>\n741-<tr>\n742:<td><code>recipient</code></td>\n743:<td><a href=\"#order-object-recipient\" title=\"Order recipient\">Recipient</a></td>\n744-<td>yes</td>\n745-<td>Shipping name and address.</td>\n746-</tr>\n747-<tr>\n748-<td><code>branding</code></td>\n--\n752-</tr>\n753-<tr>\n754-<td><code>items</code></td>\n755-<td>array of <a href=\"#order-object-item\" title=\"Order items\">Items</a></td>\n756-<td>yes</td>\n757:<td>Items to be fulfilled (products + assets).</td>\n758-</tr>\n759-<tr>\n760-<td><code>packingSlip</code></td>\n761-<td><a href=\"#order-object-packing-slip\" title=\"Packing slip object\">PackingSlip</a></td>\n762-<td>no</td>\n--\n767-<td>hashtable</td>\n768-<td>no</td>\n769-<td>A custom json object containing keys and values of your choice. Up to 2000 characters.</td>\n770-</tr>\n771-</tbody></table>\n772:<h3 id='order-object-recipient'>Recipient</h3>\n773-<table><thead>\n774-<tr>\n775-<th>Parameter</th>\n776-<th>Type</th>\n777-<th>Required</th>\n--\n803-<td>Recipient&#39;s address.</td>\n804-</tr>\n805-</tbody></table>\n806-\n807-<aside class=\"notice\">\n808:While recipient <code>email</code> and <code>phoneNumber</code> are technically optional, it's highly recommended you include these if you have international orders as they aid couriers with customs issues.\n809-For example, contact information is a requirement for any item shipped from the UK. Where necessary, we will substitute with default information if not provided to ensure courier systems accept the order, but relying on this is not advisable.\n810-</aside>\n811-<h3 id='order-object-address'>Address</h3>\n812-<table><thead>\n813-<tr>\n--\n819-</thead><tbody>\n820-<tr>\n821-<td><code>line1</code></td>\n822-<td>string</td>\n823-<td>yes</td>\n824:<td>First line of recipient&#39;s address.</td>\n825-</tr>\n826-<tr>\n827-<td><code>line2</code></td>\n828-<td>string</td>\n829-<td>no</td>\n830:<td>Second line of recipient&#39;s address.</td>\n831-</tr>\n832-<tr>\n833-<td><code>postalOrZipCode</code></td>\n834-<td>string</td>\n835-<td>yes</td>\n836:<td>Postcode or zip code of recipient&#39;s address.</td>\n837-</tr>\n838-<tr>\n839-<td><code>countryCode</code></td>\n840-<td>string</td>\n841-<td>yes</td>\n842:<td>Two-letter <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_ISO_3166_country_codes\" title=\"ISO country code list\">ISO country code</a> of recipient&#39;s address.</td>\n843-</tr>\n844-<tr>\n845-<td><code>townOrCity</code></td>\n846-<td>string</td>\n847-<td>yes</td>\n848:<td>Town or city of recipient&#39;s address.</td>\n849-</tr>\n850-<tr>\n851-<td><code>stateOrCounty</code></td>\n852-<td>string</td>\n853-<td>no</td>\n854:<td>State or county for the recipient&#39;s address.</td>\n855-</tr>\n856-</tbody></table>\n857-<h3 id='order-object-branding'>Branding</h3>\n858:<p>The <code>branding</code> object allows you to specify one or more branded assets (e.g. postcards, flyers, stickers, and packing slips) that will be included in the shipment. Each item must be supplied as a URL pointing to a publicly accessible asset.</p>\n859-\n860-<p>Additional file setup details including pricing for each item can be found within your <a href=\"https://dashboard.prodigi.com/settings/branding\">Prodigi account</a>.</p>\n861-\n862-<table><thead>\n863-<tr>\n--\n927-</thead><tbody>\n928-<tr>\n929-<td><code>url</code></td>\n930-<td>string</td>\n931-<td>Yes</td>\n932:<td>A publicly accessible URL pointing to print-ready assets. Each asset will be validated for format and quality.</td>\n933-</tr>\n934-</tbody></table>\n935-<h3 id='order-object-charge'>Charge</h3>\n936-<table><thead>\n937-<tr>\n--\n1159-</tr>\n1160-<tr>\n1161-<td><code>status</code></td>\n1162-<td>string</td>\n1163-<td>n/a</td>\n1164:<td>A status indicator for the item expected values are: <code>Ok</code> nothing wrong with this item, <code>Invalid</code> one or more assets have failed to download and <code>NotYetDownloaded</code> the assets associated with this item are yet to be downloaded.</td>\n1165-</tr>\n1166-<tr>\n1167-<td><code>merchantReference</code></td>\n1168-<td>string</td>\n1169-<td>no</td>\n1170-<td>Your personal reference for this item.</td>\n1171-</tr>\n1172-<tr>\n1173:<td><code>sku</code></td>\n1174-<td>string</td>\n1175-<td>yes</td>\n1176-<td>The Prodigi SKU of the product. Use the lookups endpoints to find out more information on each SKU.</td>\n1177-</tr>\n1178-<tr>\n--\n1186-<td>string</td>\n1187-<td>yes</td>\n1188-<td>The sizing strategy for us to use. The value should be one of <code>fillPrintArea</code>, <code>fitPrintArea</code> or <code>stretchToPrintArea</code>. More information can be found in our <a href=\"#order-object-image-resizing\" title=\"Image resizing\">image resizing section</a>.</td>\n1189-</tr>\n1190-<tr>\n1191:<td><code>recipientCost</code></td>\n1192-<td><a href=\"#order-object-cost\" title=\"Cost\">Cost</a></td>\n1193-<td>no</td>\n1194:<td>The price you charged the recipient for these items. While not required, it&#39;s highly recommended if you have international orders as it aids shipping companies with customs issues.</td>\n1195-</tr>\n1196-<tr>\n1197-<td><code>attributes</code></td>\n1198-<td>hashtable</td>\n1199-<td>no</td>\n1200-<td>Product attributes, such as a frame colour. Use the lookups endpoints to find a product&#39;s available attributes.</td>\n1201-</tr>\n1202-<tr>\n1203:<td><code>assets</code></td>\n1204-<td>array of <a href=\"#order-object-asset\" title=\"Order asset object\">Assets</a></td>\n1205-<td>yes</td>\n1206:<td>File assets for this order item, i.e. the image file(s).</td>\n1207-</tr>\n1208-</tbody></table>\n1209-<h3 id='order-object-asset'>Asset</h3>\n1210:<p>An Asset is an image belonging to a product. Our products support zero, one or many images per item, and the item&#39;s <code>assets</code> array determines the location of each image on the product. For a full list of which assets a given product supports, use the product lookup endpoint.</p>\n1211-\n1212-<table><thead>\n1213-<tr>\n1214-<th>Parameter</th>\n1215-<th>Type</th>\n--\n1219-</thead><tbody>\n1220-<tr>\n1221-<td><code>printArea</code></td>\n1222-<td>string</td>\n1223-<td>yes</td>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
