{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -C 4 'lookups|Lookups|products|Products|catalog' /tmp/prodigi.html | head -260\"","aggregated_output":"5-    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n6-    <meta content=\"IE=edge,chrome=1\" http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\">\n7-    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1\">\n8-    <title>Prodigi API Documentation</title>\n9:    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"A print API for dropshipped custom products. Current version is v4.\">\n10-    <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/\" />\n11-\n12-    <style media=\"screen\">\n13-      .highlight table td { padding: 5px; }\n--\n328-    <!--OPEN GRAPH / TWITTER TAGS -->\n329-\n330-<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n331-<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Prodigi API Documentation\" />\n332:<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"A print API for dropshipped custom products. Current version is v4.\" />\n333-<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"\" />\n334-<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Prodigi\" />\n335-<meta property=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@prodigi_group\" />\n336-\n--\n753-<tr>\n754-<td><code>items</code></td>\n755-<td>array of <a href=\"#order-object-item\" title=\"Order items\">Items</a></td>\n756-<td>yes</td>\n757:<td>Items to be fulfilled (products + assets).</td>\n758-</tr>\n759-<tr>\n760-<td><code>packingSlip</code></td>\n761-<td><a href=\"#order-object-packing-slip\" title=\"Packing slip object\">PackingSlip</a></td>\n--\n1172-<tr>\n1173-<td><code>sku</code></td>\n1174-<td>string</td>\n1175-<td>yes</td>\n1176:<td>The Prodigi SKU of the product. Use the lookups endpoints to find out more information on each SKU.</td>\n1177-</tr>\n1178-<tr>\n1179-<td><code>copies</code></td>\n1180-<td>integer</td>\n--\n1196-<tr>\n1197-<td><code>attributes</code></td>\n1198-<td>hashtable</td>\n1199-<td>no</td>\n1200:<td>Product attributes, such as a frame colour. Use the lookups endpoints to find a product&#39;s available attributes.</td>\n1201-</tr>\n1202-<tr>\n1203-<td><code>assets</code></td>\n1204-<td>array of <a href=\"#order-object-asset\" title=\"Order asset object\">Assets</a></td>\n--\n1206-<td>File assets for this order item, i.e. the image file(s).</td>\n1207-</tr>\n1208-</tbody></table>\n1209-<h3 id='order-object-asset'>Asset</h3>\n1210:<p>An Asset is an image belonging to a product. Our products support zero, one or many images per item, and the item&#39;s <code>assets</code> array determines the location of each image on the product. For a full list of which assets a given product supports, use the product lookup endpoint.</p>\n1211-\n1212-<table><thead>\n1213-<tr>\n1214-<th>Parameter</th>\n--\n1250-<tr>\n1251-<td><code>pageCount</code></td>\n1252-<td>integer</td>\n1253-<td>no</td>\n1254:<td>Not required by default, but is required when creating orders containing products where additional page pricing is applied - for example: photobooks.</td>\n1255-</tr>\n1256-</tbody></table>\n1257-<h3 id='order-object-packing-slip'>Packing slip</h3>\n1258-<table><thead>\n--\n2483-\n2484-            </section>\n2485-            <section class=\"content\">\n2486-                <h1 id='quotes'>Quotes</h1>\n2487:<p>The Quote endpoint allows you to get pricing and shipping information about a given set of products without creating an order. It returns how the order will be fulfilled, including:</p>\n2488-\n2489-<ul>\n2490-<li>The fulfillment location</li>\n2491:<li>The cost of the products</li>\n2492-<li>The cost of shipping</li>\n2493-<li>The couriers of each shipment</li>\n2494-</ul>\n2495-\n--\n2550-</span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\">\n2551-</span></code></pre></div></div>\n2552-<p>The Quote endpoint returns an array of Quotes.</p>\n2553-\n2554:<p>Each Quote provides pricing information for products and shipments based on a specific <a href=\"#create-quote-top-level\">shipping method</a>.</p>\n2555-\n2556-<p>If a <code>shippingMethod</code> is specified for a Quote, only that shipping method is returned. If a <code>shippingMethod</code> is not specified, a Quote for each of the shipping methods is returned: budget, standard, standard plus, express and overnight.</p>\n2557-<h3 id='quote-object-top-level'>Top level</h3>\n2558-<table><thead>\n--\n2980-<tr>\n2981-<td><code>pageCount</code></td>\n2982-<td>integer</td>\n2983-<td>no</td>\n2984:<td>Total page count for multi-page products such as photobooks and magazines; used to calculate additional-page pricing.</td>\n2985-</tr>\n2986-</tbody></table>\n2987-<h3 id='create-quote-create-quote-outcomes'>Create quote outcomes</h3>\n2988-<p>In addition to the <a href=\"#outcomes-general-outcomes\" title=\"General outcomes\">General outcomes</a>, this endpoint can also return:</p>\n--\n3265-<td>the recommended vertical size of the print area in pixels</td>\n3266-</tr>\n3267-</tbody></table>\n3268-\n3269:                <h2 id='get-product-details'>Get Product Details</h2><div class=\"codesection\"><div class=\"codeheader\"><span class=\"httpmethod\">GET</span><span>/v4.0/products</span>\n3270:</div><div class=\"highlight\"><pre class=\"highlight shell tab-shell\"><code>curl <span class=\"s2\">\"https://api.sandbox.prodigi.com/v4.0/products/GLOBAL-CAN-10x10\"</span> <span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n3271-  <span class=\"nt\">-X</span> GET <span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n3272-  <span class=\"nt\">-H</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"X-API-Key: your-api-key\"</span>\n3273-</code></pre></div></div><div class=\"codesection\"><div class=\"codeheader\">Response\n3274-</div><div class=\"highlight\"><pre class=\"highlight json tab-json\"><code><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\">\n--\n3388-</span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\">\n3389-</span></code></pre></div></div>\n3390-<p>This endpoint returns the <a href=\"#product-details-object\" title=\"Product details object\">Product Details</a> for the requested SKU.</p>\n3391-\n3392:                <h2 id='get-photobook-spine-details'>Get photobook spine details</h2><div class=\"codesection\"><div class=\"codeheader\"><span class=\"httpmethod\">POST</span><span>/v4.0/products/spine</span>\n3393:</div><div class=\"highlight\"><pre class=\"highlight shell tab-shell\"><code>curl <span class=\"s2\">\"https://api.prodigi.com/v4.0/products/spine\"</span> <span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n3394-  <span class=\"nt\">-X</span> POST <span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n3395-  <span class=\"nt\">-H</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"X-API-Key: your-api-key\"</span> <span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n3396-  <span class=\"nt\">-H</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"Content-Type: application/json\"</span> <span class=\"se\">\\</span>\n3397-  <span class=\"nt\">-d</span> <span class=\"s1\">'\n--\n4051-<td><code>Not started</code></td>\n4052-</tr>\n4053-</tbody></table>\n4054-<h2 id='the-order-process-3-lab-allocation'>3. Lab allocation</h2>\n4055:<p>When allocating your order, we allocate to the most cost-effective lab based on the chosen products, destination and shipping method. This may require us to split the order into multiple shipments.</p>\n4056-\n4057-<p>Once this process has been completed, the <a href=\"#order-object\" title=\"Order object\">order</a> that is returned by the API shows the allocated <a href=\"#order-object-shipment\" title=\"Shipments\">shipments</a> for the order items.</p>\n4058-\n4059-<ul>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
